<title>UK: Mexico sets 500 bln lire seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>Mexico sets 500 bln lire seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Chase (books) and Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MEXICO</p>
<p> AMT    500 BLN LIRE  COUPON     8.375     MATURITY    16.JUL.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.475   PAY DATE    16.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    100.00    SPREAD	+162 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB	  DENOMS (M) 5	   SALE LIMITS</p>
<p>US/UK/IT/MX</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  MEXICO    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.625     SELL CONC  1.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND SEVEN-YEAR LIRA SWAP</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF GLOBAL EMTN PROGRAMME, NO 144A</p>
